    "name": "Arabuk",
    "system": {
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>Your companion is an arabuk, a carnivorous predator resembling a snow leopard and an elk with crystalline antlers.</p>\n<p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your arabuk shakes its head, causing a painful cacophony of sound to issue from its crystalline antlers. Until the start of your next turn, your Strikes that damage a creature within your arabuk's reach make the target off-guard until the end of your next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.companion-types.Item.Striding Strike]{Striding Strike}</p>\n<p><strong>Special</strong> Snow vision: snow doesn't impair an arabuk's vision, and it ignores concealment from snowfall. It has resistance to cold and sonic equal to half its level (minimum 1).</p>"
        },
